{"find": "[[page ?]]\n\nSTORY OF A LIFE. 357\n\nlook up at the starry heavens by night, and\n\nmorn, and noon, at the eastern, and the western\n\n_ skies, and fancy forms angelic, and white-robed\n\nsainted forms smiling with fondness down, and\n\nbeckoning me to join them. Deep too was the\n\ndelight, with which I was wont to think about all, whom I had known and loved, and who now lay dead. I summoned them before me, shades,\n\nwhose paleness was holy, beautifully holy to me.", "replace": "[[page 357]]\n\n[[cont]]look up at the starry heavens by night, and morn, and noon, at the eastern, and the western skies, and fancy forms angelic, and white-robed sainted forms smiling with fondness down, and beckoning me to join them. Deep too was the delight, with which I was wont to think about all, whom I had known and loved, and who now lay dead. I summoned them before me, shades, whose paleness was holy, beautifully holy to me."}
